# ── CAWS governance state and managed runtime (byte-stable by design) ──────
# .caws/ holds CLI-written, audit-chained governance state — specs, waivers,
# policy, events — plus the live project-wired hook runtime. The CLI is the sole
# writer of spec YAML; a formatter rewriting it bypasses the audit trail. Before
# this entry, lint-staged reformatted any spec YAML that happened to be staged.
.caws/

# Hook-pack templates and their installed copies carry CAWS-MANAGED headers and
# feed a pack fingerprint: sha256 over the sorted [relpath, contentHash] pairs,
# compared against a recorded baseline. Any reflow shifts that fingerprint,
# which forces a pack version bump and re-propagation to every consumer, so a
# formatting pass must never reach them.
packages/caws-cli/templates/hook-packs/
.claude/hooks/
.opencode/plugins/
.kimi-code/AGENTS.md
.opencode/AGENTS.md
.qwen/CAWS-HOOKS.md

# ── Generated artifacts (the generator owns their formatting) ──────────────
# Each has a --check or conformance gate that byte-compares generator output
# against the committed file; formatting them makes that gate fail.
*.generated.ts
docs/command-reference.md
packages/caws-cli/docs/command-reference.md

# Docs carrying populate-doc-markers.mjs generated blocks. The generator and
# prettier do not converge: reformatting the injected block makes
# `populate-doc-markers.mjs --check` report STALE, and re-running the generator
# reproduces a block prettier wants to reflow again. The generator owns these
# files until it emits prettier-stable output.
packages/caws-cli/README.md
packages/caws-cli/templates/CLAUDE.md
packages/caws-cli/templates/agents.md
docs/guides/agent-integration-guide.md
